{"type":"message","id":"6494b9b0","parentId":"0d2ffa7f","timestamp":"2026-04-29T17:31:56.973Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Zeeshan wants to learn about crypto scalping. \nScalping is high-frequency, short-term trading.\nI need to explain it simply, safely, and warn him about the risks."},{"type":"text","text":"<final>Scalping is fast-paced—you're making lots of tiny trades in minutes to grab small price moves. 🚀\n\nIt’s exciting but honestly pretty risky, especially for beginners. Before you dive in, here’s the game plan:\n\n1. **Pick a reliable exchange:** You need one with *very* low trading fees (high fees will eat your profits).\n2. **Focus on liquid assets:** Stick to major coins like BTC or ETH so you can enter/exit trades instantly.\n3. **Use 1-minute or 5-minute charts:** You’ll be looking at super short-term trends.\n4. **Learn Technical Analysis:** You need to understand indicators like RSI, Bollinger Bands, or Volume to spot quick entries.\n5. **Strict Discipline:** You *must* have a stop-loss for every trade. If a trade goes wrong, get out fast—don't \"hope\" for a turnaround.\n\n**Serious warning:** Most scalpers lose money because of emotions and high fees. Start with a \"paper trading\" (fake money) account first to practice your strategy without risking your actual cash! 💸\n\nWant me to help you find a good guide or a simulator to practice on?</final>"}],"api":"google-generative-ai","provider":"google","model":"gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview","usage":{"input":11404,"output":312,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11716,"cost":{"input":0.002851,"output":0.000468,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.003319}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1777483903710,"responseId":"i0Dyaa3RKJPKvdIPso6lyQU"}}
